WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.419 --> 00:00:08.990
This is a quick demonstration of how to easily
select a chromosome region while using NCBI's

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.910
Genome Data Viewer, GDV.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:17.400
I'll start on the GDV home page, with human
selected, but this capability is available

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:22.440
for all organisms that have completely assembled
chromosomes.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:27.600
I'll open the viewer's display by clicking
on Browse genome, for the latest Assembly,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.730
GRCh38.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:34.600
By default, all of chr 1 is displayed.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:41.079
You can change chromosomes in the Ideogram
View,

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:46.120
or in the pull-down menu above the Chromosome
Region Selector, which is the focus of this

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.120
video.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.010
And, if you suddenly remember that you really
wanted the previous assembly, you can change

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:55.209
that here as well.

00:00:55.209 --> 00:00:59.219
For a few organisms you'll see this cytogenetic
banding.

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:05.740
If you want to view the q24 region, for example,
simply click inside the region to select it,

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:09.100
and the display below zooms to that region.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.030
Of course you can click and drag to select
any part of the chromosome.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:17.729
Then click and drag the ends of the selection
window to resize it.

00:01:17.729 --> 00:01:24.299
For organisms curated by the Genome Reference
Consortium, human, mouse, zebrafish and chicken,

00:01:24.299 --> 00:01:28.530
curation regions like patches are annotated
under the chromosome.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.250
Hover over a marked region to get more information.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:36.890
Then, in the popup, you can click on the Region
name to zoom to that region.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:43.010
If you click on the RefSeq for this patch,
the graphical view opens that patch scaffold,

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:46.100
this NW_003871055.3 accession.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:51.469
Clicking on the GenBank accession would open
that record in another browser window.

00:01:51.469 --> 00:01:55.790
This tool also presents green arrowheads for
search results.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:02:04.770
For example, a search for diabetes finds two
genes on chr1.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:10.600
If you want to remove those green arrowheads,
use Reset All, near the top of the page.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.989
And don't forget other useful actions.

00:02:12.989 --> 00:02:17.420
You can share the view you've created with
the "Share this page" link;

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:25.620
you can download a PDF or SVG file from the
Download menu;

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.349
and we'd love to have your feedback and questions.

